{
  "id": "ep172",
  "duration": 51.804,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 3.754,
      "text": "Critics swore the radiation belts would fry the Apollo crews.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Van Allen Radiation Belt Model shown with 2 VA Probes.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Van_Allen_Radiation_Belt_Model_shown_with_2_VA_Probes.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.767,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 3.754,
      "end": 11.049,
      "text": "In 1958, Explorer one helped discover these two massive zones trapped by Earth's magnetic field.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "America's First Satellite (Explorer 1).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA/JPL-Caltech",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:America%27s_First_Satellite_(Explorer_1).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 3.767,
          "end": 11.033,
          "kind": "cover",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 11.049,
      "end": 19.569,
      "text": "Named after physicist James Van Allen, the inner region holds energetic protons while the outer contains high-energy electrons.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "James Van Allen 72400 A78-0077-9.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Ames Resarch Center (NASA-ARC)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:James_Van_Allen_72400_A78-0077-9.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.033,
          "end": 15.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 15.0,
          "end": 19.567,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.569,
      "end": 25.889,
      "text": "Skeptics argued that passing through these radioactive zones would prove fatal for human travelers.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Apollo CSM lunar orbit.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_CSM_lunar_orbit.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.567,
          "end": 25.9,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.889,
      "end": 31.534,
      "text": "NASA trajectory planners designed high-speed routes through the thinnest parts of the belts.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Apollo 11 Crew.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Apollo_11_Crew.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.9,
          "end": 28.2,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 28.2,
          "end": 31.533,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.534,
      "end": 40.429,
      "text": "Protected by aluminum hulls and moving at roughly twenty-five thousand miles per hour, astronauts spent only thirty minutes in the dense regions.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Fisheye view of the interior of the Command Module simulator with Apollo 14 crew Ap14-S70-45580HR.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fisheye_view_of_the_interior_of_the_Command_Module_simulator_with_Apollo_14_crew_Ap14-S70-45580HR.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.533,
          "end": 36.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 36.0,
          "end": 40.433,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 40.429,
      "end": 48.104,
      "text": "Dosimeter readings revealed total radiation exposure was surprisingly low, equaling a single CT scan.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Saturn Apollo Program (8903695).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Marshall Space Flight Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saturn_Apollo_Program_(8903695).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 40.433,
          "end": 43.967,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 43.967,
          "end": 48.1,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 48.104,
      "end": 51.454,
      "text": "This thirty-minute sprint kept the crew safe, despite how",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Van Allen Radiation Belt Model shown with 2 VA Probes.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Van_Allen_Radiation_Belt_Model_shown_with_2_VA_Probes.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 48.1,
          "end": 51.8,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
